ower than your current chips.].\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Evaluation:  \nYou currently hold **7♠ 8♥**, and the board is **8♣ 9♣ A♥ 5♠ 5♥**. This gives you a pair of **8s**, but more importantly, you have a **straight draw (6-7-8-9)** and a **pair with the 8 on board**, making your current made hand **two pair: 8s and 5s** (using both hole cards: 8♥ and 7♠ doesn't help the 5s, but wait — actually, let's reassess).\n\nWait — correction:  \n- Your hand: 7♠, 8♥  \n- Board: 8♣, 9♣, A♥, 5♠, 5♥  \n\nSo possible combinations:\n- You pair your **8♥** with the 8♣ → one pair of 8s.\n- There are two 5s on the board → pair of 5s.\n→ So together: **Two Pair: 8s and 5s**, using one of your cards (8♥) and the board.\n\nAdditionally, you have **7♠** in hand. The board has **8, 9, 5, 5, A**. That means a **7 and 8 in your hand** with **9 and 5 on board** gives you an open-ended straight draw? Let's see:\n\nTo make a straight:\n- We need five consecutive cards.\n- Possible straights:  \n  - 5-6-7-8-9 → this would work! You have **7 and 8**, board has **5, 8, 9** → so if a **6** comes, you'd have 5-6-7-8-9 straight.\n\nBut wait — the **river is already out**. The board is complete: **8♣, 9♣, A♥, 5♠, 5♥** — that’s five community cards. So this is the **showdown round (Round 3)**.\n\nAh — critical: This is **Round 3**, which is after the river. All cards are out. No more draws. It's time to either bet or check based on showdown strength.\n\nSo final board: 8♣, 9♣, A♥, 5♠, 5♥  \nYour hand: 7♠, 8♥\n\nBest 5-card hand:\n- You can use both hole cards.\n- You have **8♥** → pairs with 8♣ → so a pair of 8s.\n- Board has two 5s → pair of 5s.\n- So your hand is: **Two Pair: 8s and 5s**, with kicker **7♠** (since you don’t have a 5 or better unrelated card).\n\nWait — do you need to use both hole cards? No — you can use any combination.\n\nActually, best hand:\n- Two Pair: 8s (using your 8♥ and 8♣) and 5s (from board). Then your remaining card is 7♠ as kicker.\n\nYes — **Two Pair: 8s and 5s,